; Lead: BrokkAi/bifrost-packs#311 (CVE-2024-1874, GHSA-pc52-254m-w9w7),
; version- and OS-independent part.
; Product source contract: proc_open runs its command. A string command goes
; through the system shell, so a request value in it can add shell commands on
; every PHP version and OS. An array command runs the program directly, but on
; Windows PHP before 8.1.28, 8.2.18 and 8.3.5 the arguments are not escaped
; for cmd.exe, so a request value in a .bat or .cmd argument also runs commands
; (CVE-2024-1874). The rule reports a request value that reaches the command
; in either form, on every runtime and OS. The Windows and runtime-version part
; of the CVE needs target and runtime evidence the engine does not have.
; Engine contract: the source is a read of the $_GET superglobal. The sink is
; formal 0 (command) of the proc_open declaration in the bifrost.php-builtin
; native pack; it binds as complete only with a pack generated by
; bifrost-semantic-pack 0.15.2 or later (bifrost-dev#9337), which certifies the
; callable family. Calls through proc_open need the reviewed
; bifrost.php-process-summaries summaries. The sink matches any call that
; resolves to that declaration, not a callee name, so a call through
; `use function proc_open as alias` is covered. String concatenation and array
; literal elements are built-in value flow. escapeshellarg, escapeshellcmd and
; every other helper on the value must be modeled, so a quoted argument leaves
; the run inconclusive instead of clean.
; Not covered: $_POST, $_REQUEST, $_COOKIE and framework request objects;
; exec, system, shell_exec, passthru and popen.
(policy
  :schema-version 1
  :id "bifrost.security.php.request-input-to-proc-open-command"
  :name "Request value reaches a proc_open command"
  :message "A $_GET value reaches the command of proc_open; as a string it runs through the shell, and as an array argument on Windows PHP before 8.1.28, 8.2.18 or 8.3.5 it can run commands through cmd.exe (CVE-2024-1874)"
  :severity warning
  :description "Reports a $_GET value that reaches the command argument of proc_open, as the whole string, inside a concatenated string, or as an element of the command array. A string command runs through the system shell. An array command is not escaped for cmd.exe on Windows PHP before 8.1.28, 8.2.18 and 8.3.5 (CVE-2024-1874), so a request value in a batch-file argument runs commands. The rule reports both forms on every runtime and OS; it does not check the target OS or PHP version."
  :help-uri "https://github.com/php/php-src/security/advisories/GHSA-pc52-254m-w9w7"
  :tags ["security" "php" "command-injection" "cve-2024-1874" "cwe-78"]
  :analysis
    (analysis
      :type taint
      :mode may
      :call-modeling (call-modeling :unmodeled require-model)
      :sources
        (endpoint-set
          :entries [
            (source
              :id php-get
              :display-name "$_GET value"
              :categories [input.user-controlled http.request]
              :selector
                (rql
                  :schema-version 1
                  (language php
                    (identifier :name "_GET")))
              :bind matched-value
              :labels [attacker-controlled])])
      :sinks
        (endpoint-set
          :entries [
            (sink
              :id proc-open-command
              :display-name "proc_open command"
              :categories [command.text]
              :selector
                (rql
                  :schema-version 1
                  (language php
                    (call-argument :formal-index 0
                      (resolved-call
                        :resolves-to "_php_global_.proc_open"
                        :proof declared
                        (call-bindings
                          (call-shape
                            (call)))))))
              :dangerous-operand (argument :index 0)
              :accepts [attacker-controlled])]))
  :classification
    (classification
      :fallback (classification-id :taxonomy "CWE" :id "78")))
